meta {
  name: List Ecatalogs
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/ecatalogs
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Accept: application/json
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.data: isArray
  res.body.data[0].name: eq Plytix Brand Portal
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-08 against "David's Dev Account". `GET` works
  fine despite creation being blocked (see "Create Ecatalog - Feature Not
  Enabled (422).bru") -- this account has one real, pre-existing
  ecatalog, "Plytix Brand Portal" (id `6a38f615c3d65a5f868b1a41`,
  read-only fixture, never mutated by this test).

  ## Real shape confirmed without needing to create anything
  Since creation is blocked, this pre-existing ecatalog is the only
  source of a real `ECatalogOutputDto` shape. Notable confirmed detail
  the spec only lightly describes:
  - `output_attributes`: each entry has `label`, `type`, `source_type`,
    `labels` (array), `formula` (a `"{{ attribute.path }}"` template
    string or, for computed ones, a nested `{"CONCAT":[...]}`-style
    object), `formatter` (a similar nested-object DSL, e.g.
    `{"DECIMAL_FORMAT":[...]}`, `{"JOIN":[...]}`,
    `{"RESOLVE_RELATIONSHIPS":[...]}`, `{"HIERARCHY_SEPARATOR":[...]}`),
    and `output_label`.
  - `settings` is a deeply nested object covering `general` (theme/
    colors/font), `header`, `footer`, `product_filters`/`file_filters`,
    `product_sorting`/`file_sorting`, `product_search`/`file_search`,
    `product_overview`/`file_overview`, `product_page` (a `components`
    array describing page-builder blocks like "Attributes grid",
    "Assets", "Variations", "Relationships"), and `attribute_usages`.
  - `assets` is a separate array of uploaded UI assets (logo, background
    images) referenced by `uuid` from `settings`, distinct from PIM
    assets.
  - Direct `product_list_id`/`asset_list_id`/`pdf_catalog_id` fields all
    present and populated on this real one, confirming the spec's direct
    cross-reference fields are accurate (unlike some other resources'
    field-name mismatches).
}
